# Application structure and layer boundaries

- Organize code by feature under src/modules/.
- Each feature may contain routes, controllers, services,
  repositories, validation, and types as needed.
- Routes define HTTP endpoints and middleware.
- Controllers handle HTTP input and output only.
- Services contain business operations and orchestration.
- Repositories contain database queries and persistence logic.
- Controllers must not access Prisma or SQL directly.
- Services must not depend on Express Request or Response.
- Repositories must not depend on controllers or HTTP concerns.
- Keep configuration and shared middleware outside feature modules.
- Do not introduce DDD, CQRS, event sourcing, or extra
  architectural layers unless explicitly requested.
- Avoid circular dependencies between feature modules.
- Do not create abstractions or files without a practical need.
